1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:04,826
This country's cooking is so
special that UNESCO protects it.

2
00:00:05,300 --> 00:00:09,096
This is Mexico, known
as the Land of Mariachi.

3
00:00:09,800 --> 00:00:11,582
Its capital is Mexico City.

4
00:00:12,280 --> 00:00:15,741
About 130.9 million people live here.

5
00:00:16,440 --> 00:00:20,804
It covers about 1,964,000
square kilometers.

6
00:00:21,500 --> 00:00:23,976
People speak Nahuatl and Yucatec Maya.

7
00:00:24,680 --> 00:00:26,931
In Nahuatl, hello is Niltze.

8
00:00:27,630 --> 00:00:30,584
In Yucatec Maya, people
greet you with Bix a bel.

9
00:00:31,280 --> 00:00:33,351
And they pay with the Mexican peso.

10
00:00:35,400 --> 00:00:36,553
Some fun facts.

11
00:00:38,017 --> 00:00:42,056
The biggest pyramid on Earth
is in Mexico, and it looks like a hill.

12
00:00:42,556 --> 00:00:46,480
The Great Pyramid of Cholula,
near the city of Puebla,

13
00:00:46,480 --> 00:00:51,058
is about 450 meters wide at its base,
and about 66 meters tall.

14
00:00:51,558 --> 00:00:54,702
Its volume is more than 4
million cubic meters,

15
00:00:54,702 --> 00:00:57,310
almost twice the Great Pyramid of Giza.

16
00:00:57,310 --> 00:01:00,187
Over the centuries,
it was covered by earth

17
00:01:00,187 --> 00:01:03,063
and plants, and a church
now stands on top.

18
00:01:03,563 --> 00:01:06,943
The axolotl, a salamander
that can regrow its limbs,

19
00:01:06,943 --> 00:01:09,867
lives in the wild in only
one place on Earth:

20
00:01:09,867 --> 00:01:12,532
the canals of Xochimilco, in Mexico City.

21
00:01:13,032 --> 00:01:16,983
And Mexico City itself was built
on an ancient lake bed.

22
00:01:16,983 --> 00:01:21,217
In some parts, the ground sinks
about 25 centimeters a year.

23
00:01:22,133 --> 00:01:24,024
Now, a few surprising places.

24
00:01:25,517 --> 00:01:28,693
Real de Catorce, on the high
plains of San Luis Potosí,

25
00:01:28,693 --> 00:01:30,368
is an old silver mining town.

26
00:01:30,368 --> 00:01:32,793
Today, fewer than 1,000 people live there,

27
00:01:32,793 --> 00:01:35,969
and you reach it through
a long tunnel in the mountain.

28
00:01:36,469 --> 00:01:41,337
Hierve el Agua, in Oaxaca, looks like
a frozen waterfall, about 50 meters tall.

29
00:01:41,337 --> 00:01:45,589
It is made of minerals, left by spring
water over thousands of years.

30
00:01:46,089 --> 00:01:49,587
Copper Canyon, in the north,
is not one canyon,

31
00:01:49,587 --> 00:01:54,128
but a system of six, with walls
that fall about 1,400 meters.

32
00:01:54,128 --> 00:01:56,807
You can cross it on the Chepe train.

33
00:01:57,307 --> 00:01:59,043
And the most surprising place?

34
00:01:59,043 --> 00:02:02,574
Cuatro Ciénegas, an oasis
of turquoise pools in a dry region.

35
00:02:02,574 --> 00:02:05,178
About 150 species live
nowhere else on Earth,

36
00:02:05,178 --> 00:02:09,230
and scientists study its tiny life
forms to understand how life began.

37
00:02:10,133 --> 00:02:12,238
So, what does $10 get you here?

38
00:02:13,683 --> 00:02:18,138
A metro ride in Mexico City
costs 5 pesos, about 27 cents.

39
00:02:18,638 --> 00:02:22,517
A taco al pastor, from a street
stand, is about $1.30.

40
00:02:23,017 --> 00:02:25,069
A set lunch at a market fonda is about $5.

41
00:02:25,569 --> 00:02:28,089
And a cold beer in a bar is about $3.

42
00:02:28,589 --> 00:02:30,833
But some things cost more.

43
00:02:30,833 --> 00:02:35,063
An authorized taxi
from the airport is about $20.

44
00:02:35,563 --> 00:02:38,882
So with $10, you get a metro
ride, a taco, a full lunch,

45
00:02:38,882 --> 00:02:41,963
and a beer, and you still
have a little change left.

46
00:02:42,867 --> 00:02:44,056
Now, the don't list.

47
00:02:45,550 --> 00:02:47,628
Don't hail a taxi on the street.

48
00:02:47,628 --> 00:02:51,785
Passengers have been kidnapped
in so-called express kidnappings.

49
00:02:51,785 --> 00:02:54,643
Take an official taxi
or a ride app instead.

50
00:02:55,143 --> 00:02:57,682
Don't leave your drink
alone in a bar or a club.

51
00:02:57,682 --> 00:02:59,639
Drinks are sometimes drugged, and the

52
00:02:59,639 --> 00:03:02,072
Canadian government warns travelers about
it.

53
00:03:02,572 --> 00:03:06,615
Don't hand your passport or cash
to an officer who asks for it.

54
00:03:06,615 --> 00:03:08,476
Corruption has been reported.

55
00:03:08,476 --> 00:03:11,299
Ask for the officer's
name and badge number.

56
00:03:11,799 --> 00:03:13,746
Don't join a political protest.

57
00:03:13,746 --> 00:03:17,453
Foreigners who take part can be
detained, or even deported.

58
00:03:17,953 --> 00:03:21,917
And don't carry a knife with a blade
longer than about 6 centimeters.

59
00:03:21,917 --> 00:03:24,445
It is illegal in Mexico,
even for travelers.

60
00:03:25,333 --> 00:03:26,497
Let's talk about culture.

61
00:03:27,983 --> 00:03:30,382
The famous dish is tacos al pastor.

62
00:03:30,382 --> 00:03:33,604
They come from Lebanese immigrants, who
brought

63
00:03:33,604 --> 00:03:36,140
the shawarma to Mexico in the 1930s.

64
00:03:36,140 --> 00:03:41,692
Mexican cooks swapped the lamb for pork,
added pineapple, and a classic was born.

65
00:03:42,192 --> 00:03:43,841
What do mariachis wear?

66
00:03:43,841 --> 00:03:47,640
The traje de charro, a tight
suit with silver buttons

67
00:03:47,640 --> 00:03:51,296
and a wide hat, inspired
by the horsemen of Mexico.

68
00:03:51,796 --> 00:03:54,657
And the classic instrument
is the guitarrón,

69
00:03:54,657 --> 00:03:57,648
a huge deep-sounding
guitar with a round back,

70
00:03:57,648 --> 00:04:00,249
that gives mariachi music its heartbeat.

71
00:04:00,749 --> 00:04:02,594
Mariachi is so important

72
00:04:02,594 --> 00:04:07,359
that UNESCO added it to its list
of cultural heritage in 2011.

73
00:04:08,267 --> 00:04:09,787
Time for a little history.

74
00:04:10,850 --> 00:04:12,160
In 1521, the Spanish

75
00:04:12,160 --> 00:04:16,940
and their allies conquered Tenochtitlan,
the capital of the Aztec empire.

76
00:04:16,940 --> 00:04:20,382
Mexico City now stands
on top of it. In 1810,

77
00:04:20,382 --> 00:04:26,011
a priest named Miguel Hidalgo called
for independence in the town of Dolores.

78
00:04:26,011 --> 00:04:28,496
Mexico became independent in 1821,

79
00:04:28,496 --> 00:04:32,809
and the cry of Dolores is still
shouted every September 16.

80
00:04:33,309 --> 00:04:36,201
And in 1910, the Mexican Revolution began.

81
00:04:36,201 --> 00:04:41,021
It ended with the Constitution of 1917,
which is still in force today.

82
00:04:41,933 --> 00:04:45,146
And now, the chapter you
were all waiting for:

83
00:04:45,146 --> 00:04:46,682
legends and mysteries.

84
00:04:48,150 --> 00:04:50,702
First, La Llorona, the weeping woman.

85
00:04:50,702 --> 00:04:55,048
In the legend, a woman in white
walks along the water at night,

86
00:04:55,048 --> 00:04:57,048
crying for her lost children.

87
00:04:57,548 --> 00:05:00,891
They say she drowned them, and now
searches for them forever.

88
00:05:00,891 --> 00:05:04,508
Many people claim to hear her cries
near the canals of Xochimilco.

89
00:05:05,008 --> 00:05:08,965
Some say the story goes back
to an omen before the Spanish arrived,

90
00:05:08,965 --> 00:05:12,214
a woman heard crying in the night
in the Aztec capital.

91
00:05:12,214 --> 00:05:14,695
Nobody knows where the legend truly began.

92
00:05:15,195 --> 00:05:19,108
Next, the Island of the Dolls,
in the canals of Xochimilco.

93
00:05:19,108 --> 00:05:24,149
Hundreds of old dolls hang from the trees,
their faces broken and weathered.

94
00:05:24,649 --> 00:05:29,692
The story says a man named Julián Santana
hung them to calm the spirit of a girl

95
00:05:29,692 --> 00:05:30,889
who drowned nearby.

96
00:05:30,889 --> 00:05:33,789
He reportedly died in 2001,
in the same canal.

97
00:05:34,289 --> 00:05:36,254
Locals say the dolls whisper at night.

98
00:05:36,254 --> 00:05:38,787
But nobody has ever proved
the story of the girl.

99
00:05:39,287 --> 00:05:43,691
And finally, the Zone of Silence,
in the Mapimí region, in the north.

100
00:05:43,691 --> 00:05:47,392
The legend says radios fail
there, and compasses go crazy.

101
00:05:47,892 --> 00:05:52,273
In 1970, a United States test
rocket really did crash nearby,

102
00:05:52,273 --> 00:05:54,500
which fed the rumors for years.

103
00:05:55,000 --> 00:05:58,145
But scientists have never
confirmed any strange effect.

104
00:05:58,145 --> 00:06:01,805
So, is the Zone of Silence a mystery,
or just a very good story?

105
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:06,221
That was Mexico.

106
00:06:06,471 --> 00:06:08,131
Which country should we visit next?

107
00:06:08,131 --> 00:06:09,269
Tell me in the comments.
